  "description": "This walk visits Errit Lough in west County Roscommon. The lake is located 10 km south-west of the town of Ballaghaderreen in the upper part of the Boyle River catchment.  On the western side of the lake you will find a parking area with picnic tables where you can enjoy a fine view of the lake. Here you can also pick up a footpath heading north west along the water towards a woodland area. It's a pleasant place for a very peaceful stroll with interesting vegetation, geological features and wildlife to look out for.To continue your lakeside walking in the area head toLough O' Flynn.",
